<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 1: Introduction to Securities (Weightage: 3%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">This foundational chapter introduces the overarching landscape of the Indian securities market. Candidates must understand the fundamental function of the financial system, the flow of capital from savers to borrowers, and the distinct roles of the primary and secondary markets.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 2: Characteristics of Equity Shares (Weightage: 6%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">Equity forms the core of corporate capital. You will be evaluated on your understanding of shareholder rights, voting mechanisms, face value versus market value, and corporate actions such as dividend declarations, bonus issues, and stock splits. Our NISM II A Demo Test ensures your grasp of these fundamental equity characteristics is flawless.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 3: Characteristics of Debt Securities (Weightage: 6%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
RTAs manage not just shares, but also corporate bonds and debentures. This module covers the features of debt instruments, including coupon rates, maturity dates, secured versus unsecured debt, and the crucial role of Debenture Trustees in safeguarding investor interests.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 4 & 5: Other Securities and Basics of Mutual Funds (Combined Weightage: 6%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
These chapters broaden your product knowledge. You will explore preference shares, warrants, and convertible instruments. Additionally, candidates receive an introduction to the structure of mutual funds, understanding how Asset Management Companies (AMCs) interact with RTAs for unit allocation and redemption processes.
</p>

<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 6: SEBI – Role and Regulations (Weightage: 14%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
This is one of the most critical segments of the examination. Carrying a massive 14% weightage, this chapter evaluates your knowledge of the regulatory environment. You must master the SEBI Act, 1992, the Securities Contracts (Regulation) Act, 1956, and the Depositories Act, 1996. Furthermore, you will be rigorously tested specifically on the SEBI (Registrars to an Issue and Share Transfer Agents) Regulations, 1993. A robust NISM Registrars to an Issue and Share Transfer Agents (Corporate) Certification Model Test will heavily emphasise the code of conduct, registration requirements, and capital adequacy norms for RTAs.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 7, 8, & 9: Public Offerings and Allotment Processes (Combined Weightage: 15%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
Taking a company public is a highly complex logistical operation managed largely by the RTA. This section delves deeply into the SEBI (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations. You must possess a comprehensive understanding of Initial Public Offerings (IPOs), Follow-on Public Offers (FPOs), Rights Issues, and Private Placements.<br><br>
Candidates will be tested heavily on the Application Supported by Blocked Amount (ASBA) process, the finalisation of the basis of allotment, and the strict timelines for refunding unallotted funds. Preparing with comprehensive NISM II A Mock Test Papers is essential for mastering this procedural terminology.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 10: Roles and Responsibilities in a Public Issue (Weightage: 6%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
An IPO is a collaborative effort. This chapter requires you to understand how the RTA coordinates with the Book Running Lead Managers (Merchant Bankers), Syndicate Members, Escrow Collection Banks, and Underwriters to ensure a successful listing.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 11 & 12: Depositories and Related Processes (Combined Weightage: 22%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
This represents the highest combined weightage in the entire syllabus. The modern Indian market is entirely paperless. You must master the operational workflows of the National Securities Depository Limited (NSDL) and the Central Depository Services Limited (CDSL).
You will face intricate questions regarding the dematerialisation (converting physical certificates to electronic form) and rematerialisation processes. Furthermore, candidates must flawlessly understand the RTA's role in reconciling electronic balances with the issued capital of the company. Our NISM II A Registrars to an Issue and Share Transfer Agents (Corporate) Certification Mock Test dedicates an extensive portion of its database to these high-weightage depository mechanisms.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 13: Investor Interface with the R&T Agent (Weightage: 10%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
RTAs are the primary point of contact for investors. This critical module covers the handling of investor requests, including the transmission of shares (in case of death), transposition, change of address, and updating bank mandates. You must understand the strict turnaround times (TAT) mandated by SEBI for processing these requests.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 14 & 15: Secondary Market Transactions and Client Servicing (Combined Weightage: 12%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
The final section reinforces the operational realities of post-issue activities. It covers how RTAs manage the secondary market transfer of physical shares (where still applicable), the calculation and disbursement of dividends, and the management of the Investor Education and Protection Fund (IEPF). Finally, you will be evaluated on the SEBI SCORES portal and the mechanisms for resolving investor grievances efficiently. A highly accurate NISM 2A Demo Test ensures you memorise these vital client servicing protocols perfectly.</p>


